# Lab Grown Marquise Diamond ({{year}}): 4 Sizes That Beat Natural Price

![Three marquise cut lab grown diamonds held in jeweler tweezers against a grey backdrop with text overlay reading Lab Grown Marquise Diamond 4 Sizes That Beat Natural Price as the DiamondCritics featured image for the lab grown marquise diamond guide](/images/lab-grown-marquise-diamond.jpg "Lab Grown Marquise Diamond 4 Sizes That Beat Natural Price")

## TL;DR — Lab Grown Marquise Diamond in One Scroll

**A lab grown marquise diamond is chemically, physically, and optically identical to a mined marquise diamond.** The only difference is origin — a controlled reactor over weeks vs millions of years underground. The price difference is not small.

**The 4 sizes that beat natural price by 70%+:**
- **1ct lab marquise: $629** (IGI E-VVS2 Excellent) vs natural ~$3,000. Savings: 79%.
- **1.5ct lab marquise: $1,821** (IGI D-VVS1 Ideal) vs natural ~$7,000. Savings: 74%.
- **2ct lab marquise: $2,232** (IGI E-VVS2 Excellent) vs natural ~$32,000. Savings: 93%.
- **3ct lab marquise: $3,819** (IGI E-VS1 Ideal) vs natural ~$65,000. Savings: 94%.

**Certification in one line:** IGI = widest inventory, most competitive price. GCAL = 8X grade guarantee, 15–25% premium. GIA = rarest lab inventory, 30–50% premium.

→ Best value 1ct: **[IGI 1ct E-VVS2 Excellent at $629](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29389739?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)**
→ Best value 1.5ct: **[IGI 1.5ct D-VVS1 Ideal at $1,821](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/30145572?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)**
→ Best value 2ct: **[IGI 2ct E-VVS2 Excellent at $2,232](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/30118118?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)**
→ Best value 3ct: **[IGI 3ct E-VS1 Ideal at $3,819](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/30343375?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)**

**Priority:** For the marquise shape, lab grows the same carbon lattice as natural. There is no difference in hardness, refractive index, or brilliance. IGI and GCAL both certify lab marquise on the same scale as natural stones. See the full [marquise cut diamond guide](/marquise-cut-diamond) for shape fundamentals before you buy.

## Expert Summary

Lab grown marquise diamond pricing from certified inventory starts at **$454** for a 0.75ct IGI E-VS1 Ideal and runs to **$11k+** for a 3ct GIA D-VVS1. The sweet spot is 1ct to 2ct IGI, where you get D-E colour with VVS clarity for $629–$2,403 — stones that cost $3,000–$32,000 in natural.

I'm Farzana Hasan, a [GIA](https://www.gia.edu/)-certified diamond expert. I've graded lab and natural marquise side by side under 10x magnification. They look the same because they are the same material. The lab vs natural debate is purely a pricing question. In my consultations, the people who buy lab marquise at 2ct+ aren't compromising — they're buying a stone that a natural budget would price them out of entirely. At $2,232 for a 2ct IGI E-VVS2, you're not settling. You're buying a higher grade than most natural budgets can reach. The [IGI](https://www.igi.org/) certifications in this guide follow the same grading standards as natural stones. Full credentials at **[Diamond Critics](https://diamondcritics.com/about-farzana/)**. Our pillar **[marquise cut diamond guide](/marquise-cut-diamond)** covers every marquise topic.

This guide covers the IGI Vs GCAL Certification Gap, the 70% Floor Principle, the Lab Marquise Elongation Advantage, size-by-size pricing from 1ct to 3ct, setting pairing for lab stones, and the full 313-stone certified inventory from $454 to $11k+. All prices verified against live certified market data.

