**Verdict:** The 70% Floor holds at 1ct (79%) and rises dramatically to 93%–94% at 2ct–3ct. At 0.75ct you save 62% — good, but not a floor-beater. The 4 named sizes where you clear 70%: 1ct, 1.5ct, 2ct, 3ct.

## The Lab Marquise Elongation Advantage

**The Lab Marquise Elongation Advantage is the ability to target the ideal 1.95–2.05 length-to-width ratio at any price point without paying a natural scarcity premium for the sweet-spot shape.** For natural marquise diamonds, ideal-ratio stones are rarer and priced higher because they appear less frequently in rough. For lab, the growth process is controlled — ideal-ratio stones are not scarcer than off-ratio stones.

What this means in practice: with a natural 2ct marquise budget of $32,000, you might find 5–8 stones at your ideal L:W in the entire online inventory. The seller knows the scarcity. You pay more for shape quality on top of the carat base price. With a lab 2ct marquise budget of $2,400, you have 68+ certified stones to choose from. You can reject 10 stones outside 1.95–2.05 L:W at no cost. You filter for the best shape without competing against scarcity pricing.

A second advantage: the marquise shape has the largest face-up size per carat of any standard diamond cut — roughly 15–20% larger face-up than a round diamond of the same carat weight. Lab marquise takes this further. Your $2,400 buys a 2ct marquise that shows as large as a 2.4ct round. In natural, reaching that visual size costs $32,000 at minimum. See our [marquise cut diamond ideal proportions guide](/marquise-cut-diamond-ideal-proportions) for the full L:W and depth analysis.

