**Verdict:** The Elongation Advantage means your lab marquise budget goes further on shape quality. Target 1.95–2.05 L:W. Reject any stone outside that range — with 313 stones in inventory, you can afford to be selective. See our [marquise diamond length to width ratio guide](/marquise-diamond-length-to-width-ratio) for the full framework.

> **"The elongation point is the one lab advantage most people overlook. Everyone talks about the price. But shape quality matters as much for marquise as it does for any elongated stone — and lab removes the scarcity constraint on the ideal 1.95–2.05 L:W band completely. I tell everyone shopping a marquise: go lab first, shortlist by L:W ratio and 360-degree video, then consider natural only if provenance is a specific requirement."** — Farzana Hasan, GIA Diamond Expert

## Size 1 — 1ct Lab Grown Marquise ($629–$958)

The 1ct lab marquise is the highest-volume tier in this inventory. 17 certified IGI stones from $629 to $958 for D-E colour and VVS1–VVS2 clarity. No GCAL stones at 1ct — the GCAL 8X inventory starts at 1.25ct.

**At $629**, you get IGI E-VVS2 Excellent. E colour is one grade below D — the absolute top on the colour scale. VVS2 clarity means inclusions are not visible at 10x magnification without deliberate searching. This stone has zero visible characteristics to the naked eye. A natural marquise at E-VVS2 costs $5,000+. At comparable visual quality (G-VS2 natural), you'd pay ~$3,000. The lab stone saves $2,371 at a higher actual grade.

**At $958**, you reach IGI D-VVS1 Ideal — the maximum colour and near-maximum clarity at 1ct in certified inventory. Natural D-VVS1 1ct marquise costs $6,000+. The savings: 84%.

**What colour to choose at 1ct:** E is the practical sweet spot. D adds $329 for an imperceptible colour difference under normal viewing conditions. F saves $30 vs E with no visual difference. If you're setting in yellow or rose gold, G–H is the right call — the warm metal makes E-D colour redundant and saves an additional $150. See our [marquise diamond colour guide](/marquise-diamond-color-guide) for the full metal-to-colour pairing analysis.

